{"name":"8 Bit Eggplant","hex":"#990066","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bit","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Berinomo."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small amount of something.","A piece of metal placed in a horse's mouth and connected to the reins to direct the animal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bit"},{"term":"eggplant","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The plant Solanum melongena or its edible fruit; an aubergine.","A dark purple color, like that of the skin of this fruit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eggplant"}],"entries":[{"title":"8-bit computing","blocks":[{"text":"In computer architecture, 8-bit integers or other data units are those that are 8 bits wide. Also, 8-bit central processing unit (CPU) and arithmetic logic unit (ALU) architectures are those that are based on registers or data buses of that size. Memory addresses for 8-bit CPUs are generally larger than 8-bit, usually 16-bit. 8-bit microcomputers are microcomputers that use 8-bit microprocessors."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/8-bit_computing","wikidata":"Q270159"},{"title":"8","blocks":[{"text":"8 (eight) is the natural number following 7 and preceding 9."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/8","wikidata":"Q23355"},{"title":"Bit","blocks":[{"text":"The bit is the most basic unit of information in computing and digital communication. The name is a portmanteau of binary digit. Its symbol is either \"bit\" or lowercase \"b\". Use of the latter may create confusion with capital \"B\", which is the international standard symbol for the byte."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bit","wikidata":"Q8805"},{"title":"Eggplant","blocks":[{"text":"Solanum melongena is a plant species in the nightshade family Solanaceae, grown worldwide for its edible fruit, typically used as a vegetable in cooking. It is known by a number of names, including eggplant, aubergine,